# Dev-provenance docs stay in the repo but are excluded from release archives
# (`git archive`) — ~240KB of internal review history, not needed to run the kit.
DECISIONS.md export-ignore

# The website — source and built output — is 1.3 MB of the 7.8 MB tracked here
# and is of no use to anyone installing the kit. It stays on this branch rather
# than moving to its own, and the reason is worth writing down: twenty-six of
# the site's tests derive their expectations from the KIT (how many tools are in
# scripts/, how many hooks are registered, which version CITATION.cff declares),
# so a site branch would have to carry the kit too. It would not separate the
# two, it would duplicate one of them and add a permanent obligation to merge
# and rebuild before the site's own suite could pass again — for 17% of a
# checkout. `export-ignore` gets the same bytes out of `git archive`, which is
# what "Download ZIP" and every release tarball are, at the cost of one line
# each and no ongoing sync.
#
# It does NOT shrink a `git clone`. Nothing but a branch split would, and that
# is the trade being declined here rather than overlooked.
web/    export-ignore
docs/   export-ignore
